@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: List Shares Command
  "CLI handler for mason ls: columnar or JSON listing from the local manifest cache."

  Provides:
    - cli.newLsCommand @source("symbol:newLsCommand")
    - cli.defaultLsRun @source("symbol:defaultLsRun")
    - cli.buildShareRows @source("symbol:buildShareRows")
    - cli.renderTable @source("symbol:renderTable")

  Consumes:
    - cli.shareStack
    - cli.remoteSync
    - remote.LocalCache.Read
    - domain.Manifest

  Invariants:
    - defaultLsRun MUST best-effort sync cache then read from LocalCache
    - Optional prefix MUST filter by object-path prefix only
    - Rows MUST sort deterministically by object path then slug
    - Plain output MUST use a fixed columnar grid greppable without JSON

  Scenario (happy-path): List all shares
    Given a cached manifest with shares
    When mason ls runs
    Then columnar PATH SLUG SIZE HASH SHARED STATE rows are printed

  Scenario (happy-path): Prefix filter
    Given shares under inbox/ and super/
    When mason ls inbox runs
    Then only inbox/ paths appear

  Scenario (happy-path): Empty manifest
    Given no shares
    When mason ls runs without --quiet
    Then No shares. is printed

  Scenario (negative): Cache read failure
    Given LocalCache.Read returns an error
    When defaultLsRun runs
    Then the command fails before rendering
